---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { BRAND } from '../config';
const UPDATED = 'October 12, 2026';
---

<Base
  title={`Terms of Service | ${BRAND}`}
  description={`${BRAND} Terms of Service: the free browser-side resume matcher, the optional paid AI rewrite feature, credit packs, refunds, and acceptable use.`}
  path="/terms"
>
  <section class="prose">
    <h1>Terms of Service</h1>
    <p class="lead">Last updated: {UPDATED}</p>

    <h2>1. Who we are</h2>
    <p>
      {BRAND} ("we", "the service") is a resume-tailoring web application operated by ZHANG Lei (individual,
      China). You can reach us at <a href="mailto:support@tailorresume.dev">support@tailorresume.dev</a>.
      Payments are processed by Creem, our Merchant of Record.
    </p>

    <h2>2. The service</h2>
    <p>
      {BRAND} has two parts. (a) A <b>free keyword matcher</b> that compares a resume with a job description
      entirely in your browser; the text you paste is never uploaded for this feature. (b) An <b>optional AI
      rewrite feature</b> that sends the resume and job description you pasted to our API and a third-party
      language-model provider (DeepSeek) to produce a tailored version. These terms cover both.
    </p>

    <h2>3. Accounts</h2>
    <p>
      You can use the matcher without an account. Signing in with Google is optional and unlocks
      account-based free quota and credit packs. You are responsible for keeping your Google account secure
      and for activity that happens under your sign-in.
    </p>

    <h2>4. Free quota and paid credits</h2>
    <p>
      You get 3 free AI rewrites per account (and 3 per anonymous device before signing in). After that, AI
      rewrites consume <b>credits</b>: 5 credits for $1.99, or 30 credits for $9.00. One credit is consumed
      per rewrite request. Credits are personal to your account, cannot be transferred, and do not expire.
      Current prices are always published on our <a href="/pricing">Pricing page</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>5. Payment</h2>
    <p>
      Credit packs are one-time purchases — there is no subscription and no auto-renewal. Checkout and
      payment are handled by Creem as Merchant of Record; Creem charges your payment method, issues invoices,
      and handles applicable taxes. We never receive your full card details. Prices may change in the future,
      but changes never affect credits you have already purchased.
    </p>

    <h2>6. Refunds</h2>
    <p>
      If a purchase did not work as described, contact
      <a href="mailto:support@tailorresume.dev">support@tailorresume.dev</a> within 14 days of purchase and we
      will refund credits that remain unused, in full. Credits already consumed are non-refundable, because
      each rewrite costs us server money the moment it runs. You can also request refunds through Creem.
    </p>

    <h2>7. Acceptable use</h2>
    <p>
      You agree to use the service lawfully and honestly. The full rules are in our
      <a href="/acceptable-use">Acceptable Use Policy</a>. In short: don't use the AI rewrite to fabricate
      credentials, don't upload content you have no right to use, don't abuse or automate the service, and
      don't request content that is illegal, hateful, or sexually explicit.
    </p>

    <h2>8. AI output — no guarantees</h2>
    <p>
      The AI rewrite rephrases the facts <b>you</b> provide and can make mistakes or omissions. We do not
      guarantee job interviews, hiring outcomes, ATS results, or any specific score improvement. You must
      review every line before sending a rewritten resume anywhere — you own the truth of your document.
      Fabricating experience or credentials in a job application is your responsibility, not ours, and is
      prohibited by our Acceptable Use Policy.
    </p>

    <h2>9. Your content</h2>
    <p>
      You keep all rights to the resume and job description you paste. We process them only to produce your
      rewrite and to operate quota/billing; we do not sell them or train models on them. See the
      <a href="/privacy">Privacy page</a> for exactly what is and isn't stored.
    </p>

    <h2>10. Intellectual property</h2>
    <p>
      The {BRAND} website, matcher logic, and branding are owned by the operator and protected by applicable
      intellectual-property law. You may not copy, mirror, or resell the service without written permission.
    </p>

    <h2>11. Availability and warranties</h2>
    <p>
      The service is provided "as is". We aim for high availability but do not warrant uninterrupted or
      error-free operation, and we may change or discontinue features. To the maximum extent permitted by
      law, we disclaim implied warranties of merchantability and fitness for a particular purpose.
    </p>

    <h2>12. Limitation of liability</h2>
    <p>
      To the maximum extent permitted by law, our total liability arising from the service or any purchase is
      limited to the amount you paid us in the 12 months before the claim (for free users, zero). We are not
      liable for indirect or consequential damages, including lost job opportunities. Nothing in these terms
      limits liability that cannot be limited by law.
    </p>

    <h2>13. Suspension and termination</h2>
    <p>
      We may suspend or terminate accounts that violate these terms or the Acceptable Use Policy. If we
      terminate a paid account without cause, we refund unused credits. You can stop using the service at any
      time; contact us to delete your account data.
    </p>

    <h2>14. Changes to these terms</h2>
    <p>
      We may update these terms as the service evolves. Material changes will be announced on the site, and
      the "last updated" date above always reflects the current version. Continuing to use the service after
      a change means you accept the updated terms.
    </p>

    <h2>15. Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Questions about these terms: <a href="mailto:support@tailorresume.dev">support@tailorresume.dev</a>.
      These terms don't reduce any mandatory consumer rights you have under the law where you live.
    </p>
  </section>
</Base>
